0. Meta-finding: the score you're competing on
Gemini kept conflating two metrics and that confusion drove bad decisions.

Metric	What it is	Where it comes from
In-game cash (env.state[i].reward)	Your player's money at turn 720	Local sim only
Leaderboard rating	Trueskill/Elo-style skill rating, starts ~600	Kaggle eval pool
A 3,753 in-game cash run does not predict a 3,753 leaderboard score. On a new
submission against the global pool you start at baseline rating (~600) and the
rating moves up/down based on wins and losses against other bots. Your 600 → 516
drop is normal for a new bot, and has nothing to do with "the math being
broken" — it just means you lost your first rated matches.

Why you lost: you trained against "random", which is genuinely useless. The
real leaderboard is full of people who also read the source, who also have
