No weather system. Plants die from un-watering, not drought. ✅
Random weed spawn rate is 0.5%/empty tile/night (default
weedSpawnChance). ✅
⚠️ Half-right / oversold
"There is no weather system" — true, but Gemini then claimed your farmer
had to physically walk to each tile. Correct, but the implication that
other bots aren't doing this is wrong. Top bots all do this. You're not
exploiting a secret.
"Animals can't be sold" — partial. The game code has no SELL_LIVESTOCK
action at all; the only "sell" surface is SELL <item> and animals aren't
in the PRODUCTS list, so the engine silently no-ops. Your old "FIRE_ALL_LABOR"
market action likewise doesn't exist — that string is not a recognized market
order. The interpreter drops unknown orders. None of that was a "trap" — it
was the engine quietly ignoring nonsense.
Tomato/Strawberry yields: Gemini said "1 unit every day" for Tomato and
"every other day" for Strawberry. The actual values: Tomato interval=1
(daily) ✅, Strawberry interval=2 (every other day) ✅, but both cap at 4
scheduled yields total, then decay. The chat didn't tell you about the
decay phase, so if you plant tomatoes at day 25 you'll get at most 1 yield
before they rot.
❌ Wrong / fabricated
The "3.60 multiplier on melons" / "logarithmic curve on wheat" pitch.
Gemini did get the function names right by accident, but the marketing
around it ("brutal penalty multiplier 3.60 — overproducing will tank value
instantly") is exaggerated. The actual MARKET_PARAMS table says Melon
