them to the floor" — partially right (melon, strawberry, milk, wool do
have above_target ≥ 1.6), but the chat didn't make clear that wheat and
eggs are the only crops that absorb gluts (log curve), so dumping wheat
on a saturated market barely moves the price. This is the actual "stable
staple" insight Gemini fumbled.
The CARROT note from "God-Mode" (Day 2 first yield, Day 3 max, 3 units
