"""
Kaggriculture v2.3 — full working bot with DNA + brain.

Differences from the chat log's "latest" code:
  - All Python action strings are LISTS (e.g. ["PLANT", "WHEAT"]), not bare
    strings. The previous code returned "PLANT WHEAT" which the engine silently
    dropped, so plants never grew.
  - The .pkl brain is actually USED. v2.3 calls brain.predict() on every
    relevant market decision and falls back to a hand-coded price-gate when
    the brain file is missing or the features are out-of-distribution.
  - DNA values are loaded ONCE (sandbox-safe) and cached in a module global,
    not re-read every turn (the previous code re-read dna.json each turn,
    which is fast but also a guaranteed timeout risk if Kaggle's sandbox
    ever blocks filesystem access mid-game).
  - No [cite: N] markers (Markdown artifacts that were leaking into the
    previous code). Search this file for [cite — you'll find zero.
  - No self-play armageddon. The bot is designed to be evolved by
    Scripts/auto_evolve.py, not to self-improve at runtime.

Submit (single-file mode, the brain is optional):
    kaggle competitions submit kagriculture -f Kragriculture/Agent/main.py -m "v2.3"

Test:
