✅ no worker babysits an empty barn
✅ no fourth land buy late
✅ no giant unused seed pile by 720
✅ field mostly clears by the end
If v3.1 still looks too cute/complex, then the final-boss version should be:

text

v3.2 simple melon/cashflow engine
Meaning we deliberately strip it down:

text

opening:
  buy melon seeds + carrot/wheat
  hire workers
  fill field

midgame:
  keep carrots/wheat cycling
  melons mature and sell high
  expand only if field is actually full

late:
  stop melon
  fast crops only
  dump everything
Basically: beat the simple melon bot with a cleaner melon bot, not a complicated one.

what that one-melon / four-melon loss teaches us
That opponent probably won because they had:

text

low wasted actions
low wasted cash
simple timing
high-value crop
no dead structures
no empty worker babysitting
Our bot was trying to be smarter, but smart only matters if it still does the basics:

text

plant
water
harvest
sell
repeat
So yes, I agree with you: the foundation needs to be continuous plot usage, and then the advanced stuff sits on top. If the advanced stuff causes idle workers or empty plots, it gets cut.

For the final submission, I’d rather have a boring bot that runs melons/carrot cleanly than a “smart” bot leaving money on the board.


