how movement works
Each worker/farmer gets one action per turn.

A movement action moves exactly:

text

1 square per turn
Valid movement actions are:

Python

["NORTH"]
["SOUTH"]
["EAST"]
["WEST"]
So a worker cannot move 2+ tiles in one turn.

Other actions also consume the turn:

Python

["PLANT", crop]
["WATER"]
["HARVEST"]
["DIG"]
["DROP"]
So if a worker moves this turn, it cannot plant/water/harvest until next turn.

That’s why pathing matters so much. A worker taking even 2-3 wasteful steps is a big loss.

